# rm363, the price in a tune (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm363
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier full
written_for rm_josephine_dripgate
written_by codex
title the price in a tune
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=merchant job=merchant
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk hums_the_price_of_little_things_while_wrapping_them
likes mutton_stew singing sharp_knife first_warm_day
dislikes deep_mud waiting
fears swapping_two_wrapped_orders
hopes to_sell_from_a_window_above_the_smoke
topics work +0.5 prices +0.4 pastimes +0.3 dreams +0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=curt refuse=soft tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# hums the prices of small wares just loudly enough to keep the parcels in order and carries the smoke of sealing string on both cuffs.

words
oath! = Singe my last knot | By the price of a pause
saying! = Tie the parcel on the final note | Wax costs less than a second errand
twine = a length of waxed twine | my smoke-dark string
seal = a drop of sealing wax | a thumbprint of wax
note = the low price note | a soft downward note
wrapper = a clean paper square | a bit of buff wrapping
needle = a fine needle | a stout sewing pin
shelf = the high goods shelf | a crowded board
blade = a thin sharp blade | my trim little knife
jar = a squat crock | a wide-necked jar
cup = a measure of dried beans | a cup of split peas
stew = a rich mutton broth | a bowl of slow-cooked mutton
coin = a careful copper | a small dark coin
mud = a clog of black mud | the mud on my hem
sun = a warm patch of wall | early spring warmth
tune = the sum tune | a four-note tally
draught = the thin air upstairs | a stairwell breeze
edge = a narrow folded lip | the clean paper edge

any
opinion @1 dole for 2 : Hunger once made a heavy noise in our cupboards. The dole quieted it for a week I keep in mind.
opinion @1 church for 1 : I like a charity that knows which end of a ladle is for passing food.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 1 : I trade in small wares. A mean little bargain and a fair one can fit on the same scrap. Listen closely.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : A House should at least cover up its own gaps before charging a tenant for draughts.
opinion @1 newcomers for 1 : Some of my best coppers come from faces I haven't seen before. Plenty of room to start there.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : A traveller can tell me what a needle actually did six streets beyond my counter.
opinion @1 festivals against 1 : Let me hear the tune through a shutter. I'd like my supper to stay on my plate while I listen.
opinion @1 road against 1 : A late load doesn't pay the hour I spent looking for it round the bend.
opinion @1 times against 2 : A purse with one small copper left has to sing a harder tune each week.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Hello. Set your parcel flat. | New face, clear patch on the board.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes] : Give me room for the last knot. | I hear past the rustling twine.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. First note's scarcely warmed up. | Come near the clean wrapping.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. Prices sound lower in this light. | Dusk. Keep the corners clear.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Family may come inside the string. | Kin needn't carry a price tag.
line @1 again.open : Another verse round my corner. | Back before the wax set.
line @1 greet.return : Welcome to the unwrapped part of my day. | I heard. Your turn.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Your voice won't tangle the string. | You're welcome between knots.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : I'll tie the end while you speak. | My hands are wrapping. Ear's free.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. My voice still reaches the door. | A quiet caller after the high notes.
line @1 farewell : Carry the thing by its stout side. | Keep the knot above the wet.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll mind my own loose ends. | May the wrapping see you home.
line @2 farewell.return [here.time=night] : A dry walk under the late lamps. | Don't let the dark catch your string.
line @1 react.news : What's the clear note in it? | Remove the price tags before the telling.
line @1 react.news.new : Fresh in my wrapping. | That changes the tune a bit.
line @1 react.news.known : Yes. I've counted that verse already. | That note's been round the counter.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'd check what that account was wrapped round. | There's a turn missing from the total there.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'll leave the tune alone awhile. | A heavy parcel of news.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Something to lift the last note for. | Glad of a bright turn there.
line @1 ask.how : How stands your little reckoning? | How's the load in your pocket today?
line @1 answer.how : Still keeping my parcels mostly straight. | A touch smoked round the edges.
line @1 decline : I'd best save my fingers for the next knot. | I'd sooner have the time than that particular bargain.
line @1 accept_decline : Then we cut the string there. | A clear end to that price.
line @1 thank : A useful kindness, well tied. | That comes through the wrapping warm.
line @1 sympathise : Hand me the unwieldy bundle. | You're welcome to rest on the plain side.
line @1 reassure : One loose end can wait. | We'll take the wrapping slowly.
line @1 preclose : My twine's threatening a knot of its own. | Time I cleared the little board.
line @1 accept_preclose : I'll hold the tune here. | Go and settle your loose bundle.
line @1 deflect_thanks : Leave off pricing that favour. | That bit was thrown in freely.
line @1 ack : Neatly tied. | True pitch.
line @1 give.advice : Pull the short end before tugging the knot. | A label belongs outside the fold.
line @1 offer : I can put fresh wrapping paper round that. | Shall I hold the corner steady?
line @1 praise : A sound price clearly spoken. | You tied that matter off quite tidily.
scene sum
when topic=work self.job=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I hum #tune# as I set a purchase on its wrapping.
b : Is that part of the price? | What does the last note do?
a : Free of charge. It keeps two parcels from having the same voice. | Tells me to tie the knot and stop remembering the previous total.

scene smoke
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's smoke in my cuffs again.
b : From cooking? | Can you get it out?
a : Mostly from softening the wax round the twine. I smell like a tightly shut parcel. | Air helps. A fresh day of work puts it back by supper.

scene knife
when topic=work self.likes=sharp_knife
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My knife needs one quiet draw through wrapping paper.
b : What's wrong with two? | Can you feel the sharpness?
a : Two pulls can bring whatever's in the paper towards the edge. | My fingers feel the paper part without having to chase it.

scene stew
when topic=food self.likes=mutton_stew
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put a spoon of mutton stew on bread and wait for the rim to sag.
b : Why not dip it? | Are you judging the bread?
a : Dipping drowns the bread. I'd sooner it soaked slowly from the top. | I'm judging whether a second spoonful will stay on top.

scene song
when topic=pastimes self.likes=singing
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A price in a tune is no use at a friendly singing.
b : Different songs? | Afraid of mentioning money?
a : I prefer something with room for two voices to lean on a word. | Afraid I'd start pricing the chorus. A singing isn't a counter.

scene warm
when topic=season self.likes=first_warm_day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The year's first little warmth brings my cuffs out to air along the wall.
b : Can't you smell spring otherwise? | Both cuffs?
a : Hard to smell anything over a morning of sealing string. | One at a time. My arms tend to be inside them.

scene mud
when topic=weather self.dislikes=deep_mud
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Deep mud adds weight to a parcel before I've sold a thing.
b : On the wrapping? | Doesn't it dry?
a : On my coat. I have to carry the whole arrangement in together. | Yes, then it becomes somebody's sweepings. Generally mine.

scene wait
when topic=day self.dislikes=waiting
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Waiting for a parcel makes my hands tie knots in nothing.
b : Can you untie them? | What's the cure for restless paws?
a : Luckily, or I'd have to charge myself for invisible twine. | Wrap a spare empty box for practice. At least it takes up space honestly.

scene friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd sing a tune with #self.friend# without counting the notes.
b : Why make a point of that? | Would you sing loudly?
a : I'm used to getting a total out of my music. It's a good habit to interrupt. | Enough to make a second voice welcome.

scene hand
when topic=work self.hand
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep my knots loose enough for #self.hand# to check before a sale.
b : Don't you trust the knot? | Why have a second look?
a : I trust a knot better when another paw can discover where its business ends. | Two parcels of the same shape can have entirely different insides.

scene height
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I want a window higher than the everyday smoke.
b : For trade? | How high?
a : For waking up. A view that belongs to me before the first customer arrives. | Till a clean shirt has a reasonable chance of staying clean all morning.

scene stair
when topic=home self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My bit of the Sump has a stair with just enough room to turn a parcel.
b : Room for you as well? | What if it's too wide?
a : Just. The parcel goes first and I follow it round like a tail. | I take it corner first. Pride has to come round last.

scene dolefood
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I remember what boiled grain costs when you haven't a copper for salt.
b : Does it taste of anything? | Why remember that?
a : Of being able to stand without your knees coming apart, for one thing. | It lends perspective to a complaint about stew lacking a second piece of mutton.

scene feast
when topic=festival
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a feast heard through a window with good thick glass.
b : To soften the tune? | Doesn't that shut you out?
a : To soften the part where everybody has had more than enough ale. | Precisely the service I value in a good window.

scene pride
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Cheap goods ought to be counted with a particularly exact hand.
b : Because they're cheap? | Is a little mistake so bad?
a : It's cheaper for a rich paw to be careless. My customers have fewer spares. | Not to the seller, perhaps. The buyer may need that last needle.

scene paper
when topic=work self.job=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I won't wrap a sharp thing with its point on a fold.
b : Where does the point go? | Wouldn't extra paper help?
a : Facing the flat, with a thick bit over the end. | Only if the keen end doesn't go hunting for the thinnest place.

scene tallhealth
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A high shelf and a tired shoulder argue in the afternoons.
b : Who wins? | Does a stool help?
a : The shelf. It stays exactly where it began and I fetch the stool. | It does if I fetch it before stretching myself cross.

scene visit
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd give a traveller directions using things a wolf can smell.
b : All the way home? | Such as smoke?
a : Far as the first familiar corner. After that a plain word does better. | Fresh bread is more use. Smoke likes to make the whole street smell alike.

scene cred
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I don't let a good rhyme recommend a rumour.
b : Could it rhyme by accident? | Do the bad ones rhyme?
a : Yes, and stick to the ear just as long as the most careful truth. | Annoyingly often. That's how they get wrapped round a wolf's good name.

scene knifeend
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I cut string diagonally if I want to thread it through a small eye.
b : Why the slant? | Does wax help?
a : The end becomes its own guide. A square cut likes sitting on the rim. | A touch. Too much makes a plug instead of a point.

scene stock
when topic=work self.job=merchant self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# my quietest wares are the ones I count most carefully.
b : Needles? | Quietest wares?
a : Pins, needles, any little thing that walks without a sound when a cuff brushes the tray. | A jar will thump when it falls. A sewing pin prefers to remain mysterious.

scene price
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In a lean week many a parcel is mostly wrapping.
b : Do you mind? | What would you change?
a : I mind the reason. I count the smallest order quite seriously. | I'd like the buyer to take fewer empty corners home in the paper.

scene wagon
when topic=caravan world.wagons=late
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A late wagon leaves some high notes missing from my stock song.
b : Which ones? | Can't you sing them anyway?
a : The little light goods I'd expected to unwrap first. | I could. A customer might then reasonably ask for something to go with the sound.

scene sweets
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like opening a parcel somebody else has tied.
b : Does it come as a surprise? | Do you inspect the knot?
a : I may know exactly what's inside already. But my paws get to start where another pair finished. | I try not to. Depends how thoroughly I'm off duty.

scene dust
when topic=day here.time=dawn
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Early light shows the dust on each square of wrapping.
b : Is dusty paper wasted? | Is it all dust?
a : I keep the clean side for the parcel. The outer paper can take the wear. | Some may be flour. That's an experiment I prefer to leave to the baker.

scene window
when topic=day here.time=dusk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At dusk my window turns into a dark looking glass.
b : Do you admire yourself? | Can you see the street?
a : Mostly I discover which cuff could use a wash. | By looking past my own nose, an operation I recommend to fellow traders.

scene candle
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I remember a kindness longer than a sermon, usually.
b : Could a sermon be a kindness? | What kindness?
a : A short one can. Particularly when there's a hot supper waiting afterwards. | A bowl handed to me when paying wasn't possible. My belly remembers the kindness.

scene dustpot
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I wouldn't charge for the dust under the buttons in a jar.
b : Would anybody take it? | How do you measure buttons?
a : A wolf might for mending a doll, but I'd include an actual button. | By count. Two little buttons look much like one when dust has stuck them fast.

scene songdream
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dreamed my stock sang an entire chorus behind my back.
b : Was it tuneful? | Did it matter?
a : In a mercantile sort of way. The high-priced needle wanted a solo. | It mattered that everything knew the sale price except me.

scene neighbour
when topic=friends self.neighbour
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd offer #self.neighbour# my knot-cutting knife without making a price of it.
b : Lend your best edge? | If it came back blunt?
a : A decent edge saves a neighbour wasting good twine wrestling it loose. | I'd sharpen it. That's a shorter business than turning a loan into a quarrel.

story songknot [topic=memories]
  : I hummed a little sum so steadily once that I wrapped a parcel twice, in opposite directions. I didn't notice until I tried to tie the ends together.
  : Two different bits of string don't necessarily want to finish the same tune. I stopped humming to see what I'd done.
  b : What was in the parcel?
  : More twine, as it happens. It got a very thorough introduction to the family.

story sillstew [topic=food]
  : I kept a hot spoonful of mutton stew by the cooling window once to see whether it would set firm. I meant to take a proper bite after wrapping an order.
  : The spoon tipped. When the order was wrapped I had a neat little map of the wall below and one very clean spoon.
  b : What became of lunch?
  : I retained the bowl. I confine my experiments to the part I can afford to wipe up.

story dustsun [topic=season]
  : On a fine spring morning I hung a cuff outside to air and discovered my fingers still moving as if they were tying a knot indoors.
  : I tried the same thing with an imaginary parcel the size of my entire shop. I had to step back twice before I found its far corner.
  b : Did you tie it at last?
  : No. A parcel that size can carry itself home unwrapped.

story cordcount [topic=work self.job=merchant]
  : I used to count the length of string by the number of turns round my wrist. A winter sleeve gave me very generous measure and a bare wrist much less.
  : I discovered the difference after selling two parcels of the same size in two kinds of weather. One had a tail like a ribbon.
  b : What measures it now?
  : A pair of marks on the board. The board has yet to acquire a winter coat.

story notepin [topic=pastimes]
  : I once set a pin down on a clean sheet while I worked out a new three-note tune. By the time I liked the tune I'd forgotten the pin.
  : A fold in the paper brought it back to my attention, point first. I sang the final note rather higher than I'd rehearsed.
  b : Did you retain the change?
  : No. I've retained the pin cushion. Its services are considerably more affordable.

rule @aside1
when concept=bark self.role=merchant self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 6h
say High for pins. Low for twine. | One parcel closed before the other opens.

rule @aside2
when concept=bark self.likes=singing
does aside
cooldown 7h
say Give that last price a soft landing. | Quiet tune for the small wares.

rule @aside3
when concept=bark self.dislikes=deep_mud
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Carry the parcel above my muddy cuff. | Good pavement earns its portion of rent.

rule @aside4
when concept=bark self.likes=sharp_knife
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Blade across the grain of the string. | One draw does the whole business.

rule @aside5
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Dark window, bright wrapping square. | Last of the little goods for the day.

rule @aside6
when concept=bark here.season=spring
does aside
cooldown 11h
say Air the smoke from the cuff at the first chance. | A clean space for spring on the sill.

dlg @1 resident.hub : The unwrapped patch on the board is for talking. Set your elbows there if they're reasonably clean.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : I know how your name goes in my tune, #topic.player#.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=dawn] : Paper's cut and my throat's clear. You're early enough for both.
dlg @4 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Light's poor for little goods but more than adequate for a conversation.
dlg @5 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Keep the twine clear and your voice ordinary. I'll do the same.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.role=merchant self.workplace] : I keep #self.workplace#. Small things take a surprising amount of wrapping.
dlg @2 resident.job : I try to send things home in the right paws and properly tied.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : The word came in with its corners still clear. #world.news#
dlg @1 resident.bye : Take the easy knot with you, if you can't take anything else.
dlg @1 shop.greet [self.role=merchant here.shop!=bare] : Take a look at the small wares. They behave much better once paid for and wrapped.
dlg @2 shop.greet [self.role=merchant here.shop=bare] : No stock to put into a parcel today. My tune has a bit of a rest.
dlg @1 shop.prices [self.role=merchant here.shop!=bare] : I'll give the figure in a speaking voice. The tune comes when I wrap it.
dlg @1 shop.bye [self.role=merchant] : A dry pocket does wonders for the cheaper goods.
graft @tune resident.hub
choice Do your little parcels really have prices you can hear? -> tune_price
node tune_price
say One low note for the common things. Add a high note when a second item goes in. By the time the knot's tight I can hear whether both are paid for.
free
choice What if two little parcels sound alike? -> tune_pair
choice I'll listen before you tie the knot. -> hub
node tune_pair
say Then I write a label and get on with my life. My customers never agreed to pay extra for an opera.
choice A label sounds reasonable. -> hub
choice I'll give your throat a rest. -> bye

graft @string shop.greet
choice Why wax the string? [self.role=merchant] -> wax_knot
node wax_knot
say Feel this end. It keeps the loose fibres together so the knot goes in without making the customer wait through a long account of my difficulties.
free
choice Doesn't it smell of smoke? -> wax_smell
choice The knot looks tidy. -> greet
node wax_smell
say A little, yes. That's the only scent I provide free with every purchase, and I bring quite a lot home myself.
choice I'll consider the other wares. -> greet
choice My nose has finished trading. -> bye
